.TH GIN 1 "November 2026" "gin 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gin \- initialize a headless file/FIFO frontend for Grappa
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gin \-\-help
.br
.B gin \-\-version
.br
.B gin init \-d
.I ROOT
.B \-n
.I NETWORK
.B \-c
.I TARGET
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gin
is an independent C99/POSIX file/FIFO frontend skeleton for Grappa's
REST resources and Phoenix Channels events. It is not an IRC client.
This version only creates and validates local filesystem entries.
It makes no network connection and sends no messages.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and the implementation boundary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the software version, not a supported Grappa protocol version.
.TP
.B init
Initialize one local target. All three options are required exactly once;
option order does not matter. No daemon is started.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " ROOT"
Absolute or relative filesystem root. Its parent directories must already
exist. Only its final component is created if missing. An existing root
must be owned by the effective user with mode exactly 0700.
Every explicit path component is opened relative to a directory descriptor
with O_NOFOLLOW; symlinks and any parent traversal component (..) are rejected.
An empty root is invalid. Dot components and repeated slashes are accepted.
.TP
.BI \-n " NETWORK"
A nonempty Grappa network slug, restricted in this skeleton to ASCII
letters, digits, underscore and hyphen, at most 255 bytes.
Network spelling and case are preserved, not inferred from an IRC network name.
.TP
.BI \-c " TARGET"
A target beginning with # is a channel; all other targets are queries.
Only # channel prefixes are supported by this local initializer.
The leading # is removed from channel directory names.
Queries use a reserved @ prefix, so #grappa maps to grappa and nick grappa
maps to @grappa. A channel named #@grappa maps to %40grappa, not @grappa.
Only ASCII A-Z is folded to a-z; there is no locale or RFC1459 folding.
All remaining bytes outside a-z, digits, underscore, hyphen and dot are
encoded as uppercase %HH. Percent itself is encoded, making the mapping
unambiguous. Non-ASCII bytes are encoded without case folding.
Empty targets, empty channel names, single-dot and double-dot names,
slash, ASCII whitespace and control bytes are rejected.
The resulting directory name must fit in 255 bytes (or the filesystem's
smaller component limit); otherwise initialization fails.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ROOT/NETWORK/WINDOW/
Directories created with mode 0700, regardless of the caller's umask.
.TP
.I ROOT/NETWORK/WINDOW/in
A FIFO with mode 0600. No reader is started: writing without a reader may
block. Do not write commands to it expecting delivery in this version.
.TP
.I ROOT/NETWORK/WINDOW/out
A regular file with mode 0600, opened with O_APPEND, never O_TRUNC.
Existing log bytes and inode are preserved on repeated initialization.
No events or placeholder messages are written. O_APPEND is an open flag,
not a filesystem append-only attribute.
.SH SECURITY
Existing directories and endpoints must have the expected type, exact
permissions (including no special mode bits), and effective-user ownership.
Endpoints must have exactly one hard link. Unsafe entries are rejected,
not replaced, followed, chmodded or repaired. Existing output entries are
checked before opening and revalidated through the opened descriptor.
Directory descriptors anchor child access; an output FIFO never causes
initialization to wait for a reader.
.PP
This is a local-user security boundary, not a sandbox against root,
a process sharing the same effective UID, hostile filesystem semantics,
or concurrent changes by the owner. Keep parent directories trusted;
permissions on ancestor directories above ROOT are not changed or required
to be 0700. Partial safe directories or endpoints can remain after failure;
initialization is repeatable, not transactional. There is no recursive cleanup.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gin init \-d ./chat \-n azzurra \-c '#grappa'
gin init \-d ./chat \-n azzurra \-c grappa
.fi
The first command creates chat/azzurra/grappa/{in,out}; the second creates
chat/azzurra/@grappa/{in,out}.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help, version, or local initialization succeeded. This never means connected.
.TP
.B 1
Initialization failed, including an unsafe name or filesystem entry.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line syntax, missing/duplicate options, or unknown command.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Networking, authentication, configuration, the FIFO event loop,
Phoenix wire encoding/decoding and end-to-end encryption are not implemented.
There is no connect, run, check, or message-sending command.
No Grappa protocol compatibility or delivery is claimed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfifo (1),
.BR tail (1),
.BR openat (2)
